1
00:00:00,265 --> 00:00:01,565
(Howard:)Hang on.

2
00:00:01,566 --> 00:00:03,866
(Penny:)Wait, you actually
think it's 2003?

3
00:00:03,869 --> 00:00:05,869
(Sheldon:)No, just because
I'm living my life

4
00:00:05,871 --> 00:00:08,301
(Sheldon:)like it was 12 years ago
doesn't mean I'm delusional.

5
00:00:08,306 --> 00:00:10,036
(Sheldon:)And since it is 2003,

6
00:00:10,041 --> 00:00:11,841
(Sheldon:)I don't know who you are,

7
00:00:11,843 --> 00:00:13,773
(Sheldon:)so please exit the premises

8
00:00:13,778 --> 00:00:16,408
(Sheldon:)before I call the police
on my stylish new flip phone.

9
00:00:28,612 --> 00:00:30,382
(Penny:)Are you doing okay?

10
00:00:30,381 --> 00:00:31,851
(Leonard:)I guess.

11
00:00:31,849 --> 00:00:34,079
(Leonard:)I'm just, you know,
worried about Sheldon.

12
00:00:34,084 --> 00:00:35,954
(Penny:)Well, come on,
he's a grown man in his 30s

13
00:00:35,953 --> 00:00:37,583
(Penny:)pretending to be
a grown man in his 20s.

14
00:00:37,588 --> 00:00:38,788
(Penny:)He's fine.

15
00:00:39,590 --> 00:00:41,960
(Leonard:)I hope so.

16
00:00:41,959 --> 00:00:43,989
(Penny:)What else can you do?
Move back in with him?

17
00:00:43,994 --> 00:00:45,494
(Leonard:)No, of course not.
I-I just feel bad.

18
00:00:45,496 --> 00:00:46,666
(Penny:)Well, so do I,

19
00:00:46,663 --> 00:00:49,033
(Penny:)but don't you want to live
with your wife

20
00:00:49,033 --> 00:00:50,563
(Penny:)and set the thermostat

21
00:00:50,567 --> 00:00:51,667
(Penny:)to whatever you want

22
00:00:51,668 --> 00:00:53,198
(Penny:)and have your body tell you

23
00:00:53,203 --> 00:00:54,873
(Penny:)when it's time to go
to the bathroom,

24
00:00:54,872 --> 00:00:55,902
(Penny:)you know, not a schedule slipped

25
00:00:55,906 --> 00:00:58,436
(Penny:)underneath your door
every morning?

26
00:00:58,442 --> 00:01:03,022
(Leonard:)I did like that he had
the weather on it.

